// Recursive handle forwarding.
//
// `build_list` returns fresh storage, so it gains a trailing arena handle as soon
// as `main` bounds the result. Its own recursive call returns what the activation
// returns: the storage that call fills is the storage this activation hands back,
// so the call forwards the handle it was given instead of passing null. The whole
// chain is one chunk, created once in `main` and released once on the way out.
//
// The parent node allocated before the recursion is not on every return path, so
// its release stays: the release runs only when the handle was null, where the
// general allocator really did hand the storage out. The arena frees it in bulk.
int* function build_list(int depth) {
    var node = memory.allocate<int>(8);
    node[0] = depth;
    if (depth > 0) {
        return build_list(depth - 1);
    }
    return node;
}

int function main() {
    var root = build_list(5);
    print(root[0]);
    return 0;
}
